        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Is Orthodontic Braces Treatment?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Crowded, overlapping, or gapped teeth are not just a cosmetic concern—they trap food easily, make brushing difficult, and can cause uneven chewing strain on gums and jaws. Orthodontic braces apply gentle, steady pressure over several months to guide each tooth gradually into a neat, balanced bite without harming the roots.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Signs You or Your Child May Need Braces</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>Overlapping or crooked front teeth that make thorough brushing tricky.</li>
            <li>Noticeable spaces or gaps between upper or lower teeth.</li>
            <li>Upper front teeth sticking forward over the lower lip (protrusion).</li>
            <li>Difficulty biting cleanly through chapati or sandwiches due to an uneven bite.</li>
            <li>Permanent teeth erupting out of line after baby teeth fall out.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Step-by-Step Procedure</h2>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12 items-center">
            <div class="sm:col-span-4 aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden img-frame">
              <img src="/images/thumbs/dental-team-shanti-dental-jaipur.webp" alt="Family orthodontic braces consultation with Dr. Shubham Gupta" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" width="640" height="480" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
            </div>
            <div class="sm:col-span-8 p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[#2A9D8F]">Family-Friendly Planning</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Clear Timeline &amp; Monthly Care for Teens &amp; Adults</h3>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">We walk parents and patients through bracket choices, expected months, and simple brushing habits before putting braces on.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ol class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base text-slate-700 list-decimal pl-5">
            <li><strong>Assessment &amp; Measurements:</strong> Dr. Shubham Gupta examines tooth alignment, jaw bite, and dental X-rays before planning space and bracket placement.</li>
            <li><strong>Fixing Brackets &amp; Wire:</strong> Smooth metal or tooth-coloured ceramic brackets are bonded cleanly to the teeth and joined with a fine archwire.</li>
            <li><strong>Monthly Follow-Up Visits:</strong> Every 4 to 6 weeks, the wire is adjusted gently to continue steady alignment.</li>
            <li><strong>Retainer Phase:</strong> Once alignment finishes, a custom retainer keeps your teeth settled in their new position.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#FFF8F8] p-6 border border-rose-100">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Benefits</h2>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Aligned teeth are much easier to brush and keep free of tartar.</li>
              <li>Balanced bite helps protect teeth from uneven wear.</li>
              <li>Improves smile symmetry and facial balance naturally.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Aftercare Tips</h2>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Cut crunchy apples, guavas, and carrots into small bite-sized pieces instead of biting whole.</li>
              <li>Avoid sticky chikki, chewing gum, and hard dry fruits that can loosen brackets.</li>
              <li>Brush carefully around wires after meals and wear retainers as advised after completion.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
