        <div data-faq-group>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30] mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="br-f1"><span>What is the best age to check for braces?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="br-f1" class="px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Most children start braces around ages 11–14, though early jaw checks at age 8–9 help spot crowding early. Adults can also get braces if gums are healthy.</div></div>
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="br-f2"><span>Do braces hurt?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="br-f2" class="hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Bonding brackets does not hurt. Mild tightness for 2–3 days after wire tightening is normal and eases with soft food.</div></div>
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="br-f3"><span>How long does braces treatment take?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="br-f3" class="hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Typical timelines range from 12 to 24 months depending on how much movement is needed.</div></div>
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden"><button type="button" class="faq-trigger w-full min-h-[52px] px-5 py-3.5 text-left flex justify-between items-center font-semibold" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="br-f4"><span>Why are retainers necessary afterwards?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-5 h-5 text-[#C1121F]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg></button><div id="br-f4" class="hidden px-5 pb-4 text-slate-600">Teeth naturally tend to drift slightly after braces come off; retainers hold them straight while gums and bone stabilise.</div></div>
